course: dictionary
lesson: 15959
title: Untidiness and words about mess
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Untidiness is a noun. It names the state of being messy and not in order. You can see how it is built: untidy is the adjective, and adding -ness turns it into a noun. «The untidiness of his bedroom made Mum sigh.» Here the untidiness is the messy state of the room.
explain: Untidiness is uncountable, so we say «a lot of untidiness» or «some untidiness», not «three untidinesses». Try the check: «There was too much untidiness in the kitchen.» If you swap in messy and it still makes sense, you have understood the word.
explain: The word can also describe work or appearance. «Her untidy handwriting lost her marks.» The untidiness is in the writing, so the teacher could not read it easily. The clues «lost her marks» and «could not read it» show the meaning before you check a dictionary.
fact: Untidiness means the state of being messy and not in order.
fact: Untidiness can also mean messy work or appearance, such as untidy handwriting or clothes.
fact: «Untidy» is the adjective, and «untidiness» is the noun made from it.
fact: Untidiness is an uncountable noun, so we say «some untidiness», not «an untidiness».
fact: Context clues, like «lost her marks», can help you work out what untidiness means before you look it up.
exercise: «The untidiness of his bedroom made Mum sigh.» What does untidiness mean here? | Being very tall | A loud, sudden noise | Being very clean and shiny | *Being messy and not in order
exercise: «Her untidy handwriting lost her marks.» Which word in this sentence is an adjective describing the handwriting? | her | *untidy | lost | marks
exercise: Which sentence uses untidiness correctly? | The untidinesses were three. | *There was a lot of untidiness in the classroom. | Untidiness is a loud, fast bus. | I untidiness the room every day.
test: Mia says, «Your untidiness annoys me.» What does Mia mean? | Your room is very clean and shiny | *Your room or work is messy, and it bothers her | You have won a prize for drawing | You are very tall and happy
test: Which check helps you know if you have understood untidiness in a sentence? | Say the word backwards | *Swap in messy or not in order and see if it still makes sense | Look only at the first letter | Count how many letters it has
exam: Ella reads, «The untidiness of the garden hid the old bench.» What does untidiness mean here? | A very bright and sunny day | A happy shout from the children | *A state of mess that hides things | A kind of bird that lives in gardens
